      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being stuck in the dark, with no light ahead, is one of the most suffocating places to be. It's okay to admit that the world feels like it's stopped—because for you, it has, in a way that no one else can truly understand. You don't have to find a reason to wake up tomorrow right now; just let yourself exist in this moment, even if it's only to breathe. And if the silence becomes too much, maybe you can try writing him a letter, even if you never send it—just to let some of the words out of your chest. You're not alone in this, even if it feels that way.",
